Demo 1- Creating a new database called 'PSTAT132' 
A database is a collection of stored information
```{r}
PSTAT132db <- dbConnect(RSQLite::SQLite(), "PSTAT132-db.sqlite")
#dbConnect opens a connection to a database- If PSTAT132-db.sqlite already exists, R connects to that database so you can access its existing tables and data. If the database doesn't exist yet, SQLite will generally create a new, empty database file with that name 
#If it doesn't exist and SQLite created a new empty database, it doesn'y automatically create the tables, you would need to create those separately

#dbExecute sends a SQL command to the database 
#PSTAT132db is the connection to the database, and the text inside the quotation marks is the SQL command the database should execute 

#dbExecute syntax is dbExecute(connection (which database to use), statement (the SQL command you want the database to execute))
dbExecute(PSTAT132db, " 
          CREATE TABLE products(
          product_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
          product_name TEXT,
          category TEXT,
          price REAL
          );
          ")
message("Table 'products' created.")
```

