Writting the tibles to the database (overwrite if already present)
This code takes the 2 tibbles we created in R, and saves them as tables inside the SQLite database
```{r}
#dbWriteTable() writes data from R into a database table 
dbWriteTable(PSTAT132db, "customers", customers, overwrite = TRUE) #"customers" is the name of the table inside the database, customers is the tibble in R containing the data to write, overwrite = TRUE means if a table named 'customers' already exists, replace it 
dbWriteTable(PSTAT132db, "orders", orders, overwrite = TRUE )
```

General syntax of dbWriteTable():
dbWriteTable(
conn, - connection name 
name, - name of the table in the database, usually written as text in quotes
value, - R object containing the data to write, such as a tibble or data frame
overwrite = FALSE, - Whether to replace the table if it already exists
append = FALSE - Whther to add the new rows to an existing table instead of replacing it 
)

- Default for both 'overwrite' and 'append' is FALSE

